## What NOT to do

- Don't hardcode role-name checks — always go through `hasPermission`.
- Don't `fetch` from a page/component — route everything through `@/lib/api`.
- Don't reintroduce a mock/`localStorage` data layer if the project has already gone real end-to-end.
- Don't introduce a native browser dialog (`alert`/`confirm`/`prompt`, `<input webkitdirectory>`, an extra `beforeunload`). See [10-frontend/error-and-loading-states.md](../../10-frontend/error-and-loading-states.md).
- Don't launch or drive `apps/web` yourself to test changes — no dev server, no Playwright/browser automation. The user verifies UI themselves; stop at `build`/`lint`/`typecheck`. `apps/api` is different — curl-testing against a locally-run dev server is normal.
- Don't cite a sibling/reference project as the reason for a design decision — justify choices on their own engineering merits.
- {{Add project-specific "don't"s as they're discovered — each one usually comes from a real mistake made once and worth preventing forever.}}
